              <strong>2. Statutory Section:</strong> Section 41 CrPC ➔ Section 35 BNSS.<br>
              <strong>3. Mandatory Safeguards:</strong> Section 41A CrPC [Sec 35(3) BNSS] mandates notice of appearance where arrest is not imperative for offences punishable under 7 years.<br>
              <strong>4. Leading Precedents:</strong> <em>Arnesh Kumar v. State of Bihar (2014) 8 SCC 273</em>, affirmed in <em>Satender Kumar Antil (2022)</em>.<br>
